<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador monetary base up 1.23 pct wk to March 14.</title>
<headline>Ecuador monetary base up 1.23 pct wk to March 14.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base rose 1.23 percent to 2.94 billion sucres ($777 million) in the week to March 14, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In February, the monetary base fell 0.38 percent to 2.84 billion sucres. It stood at 3.06 billion sucres at the end of 1996, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
